<p>Actually the Rock thing kind of goes along with what I was saying: It might not be useful to describe someone who is a little bit taller than average as tall, but describing someone over 2&#160;m as tall is a very good distinguishing characteristic. Similarly, we can assume that since its being mentioned this guy is very distinctly of African heritage, as opposed to a person of more eclectic, ambiguous ancestry, like Mr. Johnson.</p>
<p>Also added a new post to the prior discussion in the forums, regarding the artistic take on terms like &quot;African&quot; &quot;Asian&quot; or &quot;Caucasian&quot; as terms for general physical descriptions- there are pretty well established definitions in that context.</p>
<p>I've noticed you do seem to feel very strongly about the subject of ancestry and racial identity. Keep in mind, personal feelings on a subject can lead to reading more into something than is really there. (My dad's second generation Irish and he grew up in Atlantic City in the 60's and 70's. Has the scars to prove it. I get it.)</p>

